---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="FAQ | CivicConnect" description="Find answers to frequently asked questions about CivicConnect, legal information, and welfare schemes.">
  <div class="py-24 px-6 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <span class="text-caption-mono text-mute tracking-[0.15em] block mb-3">information</span>
      <h1 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-mute leading-relaxed">
        Common queries regarding CivicConnect's citations, coverage, and usage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ Accordion using native HTML details/summary -->
    <div class="space-y-6">
      
      <!-- Q1 -->
      <details class="group bg-canvas-card border border-hairline rounded-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary focus-visible:ring-inset rounded-sm">
          <h2 class="text-body-md text-ink font-medium">What is CivicConnect?</h2>
          <span class="text-mute group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-body-sm text-mute leading-relaxed border-t border-hairline/30 pt-4">
          CivicConnect is an AI-powered portal designed to simplify Indian law documents and welfare benefits for the average citizen. By asking questions in natural phrasing, users receive plain-English breakdowns supported by official citation highlights.
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- Q2 -->
      <details class="group bg-canvas-card border border-hairline rounded-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary focus-visible:ring-inset rounded-sm">
          <h2 class="text-body-md text-ink font-medium">Where does the information come from?</h2>
          <span class="text-mute group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-body-sm text-mute leading-relaxed border-t border-hairline/30 pt-4">
          All data is retrieved from official government platforms, including central and state gazettes, the National Government Services Portal, ministry websites, and legislative archives. CivicConnect does not write or issue any laws or guidelines.
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- Q3 -->
      <details class="group bg-canvas-card border border-hairline rounded-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary focus-visible:ring-inset rounded-sm">
          <h2 class="text-body-md text-ink font-medium">Can I trust the answers generated by the AI?</h2>
          <span class="text-mute group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-body-sm text-mute leading-relaxed border-t border-hairline/30 pt-4">
          We use a strict Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline which prevents the AI from fabricating answers. The assistant can only write summaries using the facts directly present in retrieved official files. Every answer is coupled with citation badges showing the source Act and Section, allowing you to cross-verify the response directly.
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- Q4 -->
      <details class="group bg-canvas-card border border-hairline rounded-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary focus-visible:ring-inset rounded-sm">
          <h2 class="text-body-md text-ink font-medium">Does CivicConnect provide legal advice?</h2>
          <span class="text-mute group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-body-sm text-mute leading-relaxed border-t border-hairline/30 pt-4">
          **No.** CivicConnect is strictly an educational and informational tool. It translates complex legal language and compiles scheme details for convenience. It does not provide legal representation, case reviews, or certified legal advice. For formal legal situations, you must consult a qualified advocate or attorney.
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- Q5 -->
      <details class="group bg-canvas-card border border-hairline rounded-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary focus-visible:ring-inset rounded-sm">
          <h2 class="text-body-md text-ink font-medium">How do I search for state-specific welfare schemes?</h2>
          <span class="text-mute group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-body-sm text-mute leading-relaxed border-t border-hairline/30 pt-4">
          In the assistant panel or schemes page, use the **Jurisdiction Selector** to toggle from "Central" to "State" and choose your specific state (e.g. Maharashtra, Delhi). The system will filter the catalog and retrieved context to state-level guidelines.
        </div>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
